# A Structure of two written forms as a requirement: a candidate with one head answers for what is used of it.
Two:
    t: (int: x 0)
    t: (int: x 0)
end: Two
One:
    t: (int: x 4)
end: One
fn: first (@: m Two) int
    return: m\[0]t\x
end: first
int: code 7
if: first(One) != 4
    code: 81
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
